13. Integration Architecture

API / Web Layer
      |
      v
Application Services
      |
      +----> Configuration
      +----> Logging
      +----> Validation
      +----> Import / Export
      +----> Health Checks
      |
      v
Repositories / External Integrations
      |
      +----> Database
      +----> Email Provider
      +----> Queue / Redis
      +----> File Storage
      +----> Payment Provider
      +----> AI Provider

Keep the package independent of HTTP request objects and framework-specific response types. Translate validation errors and health reports into HTTP responses in the web layer.

If MedOrbits also uses a Node.js backend, align the Python and Node implementations on environment variable names, schemas, database settings, and error contracts. Do not assume identical validation behavior without cross-language tests.

